From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 11:18:57 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 32/32] FIXUP: build warnings of three posted patches (clang
 -Wsometimes-uninitialized / -Wunused)

- PCI: qcom: Implement shutdown() callback (pw 1195891 v7 3/3): pcie
  stays uninitialised on the firmware-managed path but is tested later;
  initialise it to NULL.
- drm/msm: preemption aware hangcheck (pw 1196541 v2): unused ret in
  check_ring_timeout(); last_active_ctxcycles is uninitialised when the
  postamble is built without a ring (the CP_NOP payload then carries
  whatever was on the stack): initialise it to 0.
- the same hangcheck patch also leaves dev unused in a6xx_preempt_timer().

To be reported on the lists with the review; squash into the picks when
the series are refreshed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_preempt.c | 3 +--
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gpu.c             | 1 -
 drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c    | 2 +-
 3 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_preempt.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_preempt.c
